# Every Kit image is also its Kit VM's root filesystem. It needs Docker Engine
# (dockerd runs the Kit's jobs from this same image); the /bin/sh and /bin/bash
# Docker Sandboxes launches through; coreutils for the worker install; tar,
# which `sbx cp` unpacks uploads with; sed and findutils for
# update-ca-certificates, which adds the sandbox proxy's CA at VM start
# (openssl comes with ca-certificates); libc-bin for the C.UTF-8 locale
# agents' shells select and getent; and the git, curl and CA store Docker
# Sandboxes expects of a workload image. The DHI-built Engine packages carry
# no Debian copyright file: their notices are indexed by exact version in
# dhi-notices, so they are pinned here.
docker-ce=5:29.9.1-0
docker-ce-cli=5:29.9.1-0
containerd.io=2.4.2-0
bash
coreutils
libc-bin
tar
sed
findutils
git
curl
ca-certificates
